1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,874
Welcome to Sales Performance Reporting.

2
00:00:03,054 --> 00:00:10,552
This walkthrough follows a manager from a live ERP report into the supporting activity, setup and saved exports.

3
00:00:10,732 --> 00:00:14,111
The report reads the existing company database.

4
00:00:14,291 --> 00:00:23,673
It keeps quotations, actual customer purchase order receipts, ERP order confirmations and delivery challans as separate measures.

5
00:00:23,853 --> 00:00:29,861
The figures and source coverage remain provisional where the business definitions have not yet been approved.

6
00:00:30,511 --> 00:00:36,370
The journey starts with a reporting period, a comparison period and a historical cutoff.

7
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:42,493
Company viewers may also select an approved team population, teams or salespeople.

8
00:00:42,673 --> 00:00:50,141
The server checks each requested scope against the viewer's permissions; choosing a filter cannot expand those permissions.

9
00:00:50,321 --> 00:00:58,194
Named populations require a separately approved mapping, and cannot be combined with direct team or salesperson filters.

10
00:00:58,844 --> 00:01:02,308
Month View brings the selected activity together.

11
00:01:02,488 --> 00:01:10,086
The KPI cards summarize the current and comparison periods; the daily table and chart show when activity happened.

12
00:01:10,266 --> 00:01:16,449
A dash means a value is zero or unavailable, so it must not be read as a confirmed zero.

13
00:01:16,629 --> 00:01:23,952
Customer PO receipts are captured receipts, while order confirmations are shown separately as an OC proxy.

14
00:01:24,132 --> 00:01:28,461
These are not interchangeable measures or a certified revenue total.

15
00:01:29,111 --> 00:01:34,885
Weekly Overview groups dates from Monday through Sunday, including incomplete weeks.

16
00:01:35,065 --> 00:01:42,273
Team Comparison breaks activity down by team and salesperson, with a weekly team view and a weekday matrix.

17
00:01:42,453 --> 00:01:47,561
The weekday matrix can show a count, raw value or normalized value.

18
00:01:47,741 --> 00:01:54,419
Daily averages use Monday through Saturday reporting days, with configured calendar overrides applied.

19
00:01:54,599 --> 00:02:02,532
Older ERP records may use current team membership as a provisional attribution, and ambiguous owners remain unassigned.

20
00:02:03,182 --> 00:02:09,430
From the summary, the manager can inspect supporting quotation documents and their source facts.

21
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:16,873
Ordinary quotations use option-zero line details; quick quotations use their recorded price and quantity.

22
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:21,747
For older records, the document date is a proxy for issue date.

23
00:02:21,927 --> 00:02:26,266
Captured issue events provide dated snapshots going forward.

24
00:02:26,446 --> 00:02:35,443
Values in other currencies are not silently converted to Pakistani rupees, and unknown values stay unavailable instead of being filled with zero.

25
00:02:36,093 --> 00:02:39,837
Now we'll enter demo data to show how the forms work.

26
00:02:40,017 --> 00:02:46,880
We use an existing test case with no prior reporting captures, and every entry is tagged demo only.

27
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:51,379
First, we record an enquiry receipt at nine fifteen.

28
00:02:51,559 --> 00:03:00,027
Next, we record a customer-contact response at nine twenty-five, then a follow-up call at nine thirty-five with a next action.

29
00:03:00,207 --> 00:03:05,030
Each form saves to the reporting database and appears in the case timeline.

30
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:10,044
These are synthetic walkthrough records, not real customer activity.

31
00:03:10,694 --> 00:03:17,712
The customer PO form captures the case, reference, receipt date and time, and any supplied amount.

32
00:03:17,892 --> 00:03:27,610
For this walkthrough only, we use a unique demo-only reference and leave the amount blank, so the report shows a receipt count with no invented money value.

33
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:34,203
Next, an administrator can review the calculated figures and select partial with an evidence note.

34
00:03:34,383 --> 00:03:40,841
We leave that coverage review unsubmitted; demo entries do not certify full company coverage.

35
00:03:41,491 --> 00:03:50,839
Historical source figures can be previewed from a CSV and retained first as unverified observations, with their source version and evidence location.

36
00:03:51,019 --> 00:03:58,967
After source review, an eligible frozen report can be compared on the same full period, scope and end-of-day cutoff.

37
00:03:59,147 --> 00:04:05,465
A discrepancy is recorded for investigation; reconciliation does not alter the report.

38
00:04:05,645 --> 00:04:13,238
Normalized value adjustments preserve document counts and affect results only after a different authorized user approves them.

39
00:04:13,888 --> 00:04:19,157
When the scope and periods are ready, an authorized user can freeze the report.

40
00:04:19,337 --> 00:04:26,305
The saved run keeps the selected scope, periods, cutoff, calendar and supporting source facts together.

41
00:04:26,485 --> 00:04:30,259
Later changes to live records do not rewrite that run.

42
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:38,812
CSV, Excel and PDF downloads come from the same saved run, so the figures and supporting detail stay aligned.

43
00:04:38,992 --> 00:04:42,801
Access is checked again when someone loads or exports it.

44
00:04:43,451 --> 00:04:50,834
The report is connected to the local ERP database, and the walkthrough entries have been saved in its reporting tables.

45
00:04:51,014 --> 00:04:59,136
They use an existing test case and every entry is tagged demo only, including the PO example; no amount was invented.

46
00:04:59,316 --> 00:05:05,600
The report now demonstrates saved events and a counted receipt while keeping the receipt value unavailable.

47
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:15,402
Historical coverage and business definitions remain provisional, so keep these records in the demo environment and review definitions before operational use.
